---
import Gallery from '../../layouts/Gallery.astro';
import Related from '../../components/Related.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');

const rows = [
  { id: 'V-1001', name: 'Umbrella Logistics GmbH', country: 'DE', terms: 'Net 30', status: 'Active' },
  { id: 'V-1002', name: 'Globex Industrial', country: 'US', terms: 'Net 60', status: 'Active' },
  { id: 'V-1003', name: 'Acme Supply Co.', country: 'GB', terms: 'Net 14', status: 'Blocked' },
];
---
<Gallery title="Pattern: master-detail">
  <p class="demo-note">
    <strong>M2 of the four data-maintenance patterns</strong>
    (<a href={base + '/concepts/scale'}>and the most common one in practice</a>): a list
    of records, and clicking a row opens that record's fields in a panel beside the list
    or a dialog over it. A back-office user uses this all day — find the vendor, fix two
    fields, move on — and "done" means the list stays put, keeping their scroll position,
    filters and sort, while only the detail changes.
  </p>

  <section class="demo">
    <h2>The screen — side panel</h2>
    {/* A plain bordered grid, not `.bo-app-shell`: the shell is 100dvh by design,
        so embedding one in a demo forces a full-viewport box with dead space in it. */}
    <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(18rem, 1fr)); gap: var(--bo-space-4); padding: var(--bo-space-4); border: 1px solid var(--bo-color-border-default); border-radius: var(--bo-radius-md)">
        <div class="bo-data-table-container" tabindex="0">
          <table class="bo-data-table" data-density="compact">
            <caption class="bo-visually-hidden">Vendors — select one to see its detail</caption>
            <thead><tr><th scope="col">Vendor</th><th scope="col">Country</th><th scope="col">Status</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              {rows.map((r, i) => (
                <tr aria-selected={i === 0 ? 'true' : 'false'}>
                  <th scope="row">
                    <a href={`#md-${r.id}`} aria-current={i === 0 ? 'true' : undefined}>{r.name}</a>
                  </th>
                  <td>{r.country}</td>
                  <td>{r.status === 'Blocked'
                    ? <span class="bo-badge bo-badge--danger">Blocked</span>
                    : <span class="bo-badge bo-badge--success">Active</span>}</td>
                </tr>
              ))}
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <aside class="bo-widget" aria-labelledby="md-title" id="md-V-1001">
          <div class="bo-widget__header">
            <h3 class="bo-widget__title" id="md-title">Umbrella Logistics GmbH</h3>
            <span class="bo-badge bo-badge--success">Active</span>
          </div>
          <div class="bo-widget__body">
            <dl class="bo-kv bo-kv--rows">
              <div><dt>Vendor no.</dt><dd>V-1001</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Country</dt><dd>Germany</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Payment terms</dt><dd>Net 30</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Credit limit</dt><dd class="bo-amount">250,000.00 <span class="bo-amount__unit">EUR</span></dd></div>
            </dl>
            <p style="margin-block-start: var(--bo-space-3)">
              <button class="bo-btn bo-btn--sm" type="button" data-dialog-trigger="md-edit">Edit</button>
            </p>
          </div>
        </aside>
    </div>
    <p class="bo-u-text-muted">
      The list keeps its scroll, filters and sort while the panel changes — that is the
      point of the pattern, and it is why the detail is a swap target rather than a
      navigation.
    </p>
    <p class="bo-u-text-muted">
      <strong>Which row is open is carried by <code>aria-current</code> on its link, and
      the framework ships no tint for it.</strong> That is a real gap, stated rather than
      papered over: <code>data-row-state</code> covers <code>dirty</code>,
      <code>error</code> and <code>warning</code> — the states the framework owns — and a
      "currently open record" is application state, so there is no
      <code>data-row-state="selected"</code> to reach for. Add your own rule against
      <code>[aria-current]</code> if you want the row tinted; the announcement works
      either way, which is the half that must not be left to CSS.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="demo">
    <h2>The same record in a dialog</h2>
    <p>When the detail is an <em>edit</em> rather than a read, a modal keeps the user from
    losing it behind the list. Same record, same fields, different container — and the
    same <code>initDialogs()</code> wiring as every other dialog.</p>
    <button class="bo-btn" type="button" data-dialog-trigger="md-edit">Edit vendor V-1001</button>
    <dialog class="bo-dialog" id="md-edit" aria-labelledby="md-edit-title">
      <div class="bo-dialog__header">
        <h3 class="bo-dialog__title" id="md-edit-title">Edit V-1001</h3>
      </div>
      <div class="bo-dialog__body">
        <div class="bo-form-field">
          <label class="bo-form-field__label" for="md-name">Vendor name</label>
          <input class="bo-input" id="md-name" value="Umbrella Logistics GmbH" />
        </div>
        <div class="bo-form-field">
          <label class="bo-form-field__label" for="md-terms">Payment terms</label>
          <select class="bo-select" id="md-terms">
            <option>Net 14</option><option selected>Net 30</option><option>Net 60</option>
          </select>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="bo-dialog__footer">
        <button class="bo-btn bo-btn--secondary" type="button" data-dialog-close>Cancel</button>
        <button class="bo-btn" type="button" data-dialog-close>Save</button>
      </div>
    </dialog>
    <p class="bo-u-text-muted">
      <strong>Zero new CSS.</strong> This pattern is the
      <a href={base + '/components/data-table'}>data table</a>, a
      <a href={base + '/components/dashboard#card'}>card</a> as the panel,
      <a href={base + '/components/kv'}>key-value facts</a> for the read view, and
      <a href={base + '/components/dialog'}>dialog</a> or
      <a href={base + '/components/offcanvas'}>offcanvas</a> as the container. There is no
      <code>.bo-master-detail</code>, and there should not be.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="demo">
    <h2>Which container — and this is the decision that goes wrong</h2>
    <div class="bo-data-table-container" tabindex="0">
      <table class="bo-data-table" data-density="compact">
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Use</th><th scope="col">When</th><th scope="col">Why not the others</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">Side panel</th>
            <td>reading and light edits, and the user compares records</td>
            <td>keeps the list visible, so "next record" costs one click and no context</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">Dialog</th>
            <td>a focused edit that must be finished or abandoned</td>
            <td>modality is the feature — it stops a half-edited record being forgotten behind the list</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">Full page</th>
            <td>the record has its own tabs, attachments and audit trail</td>
            <td>a panel that needs to scroll independently and hold tabs is a page wearing a costume — use <a href={base + '/patterns/record-detail'}>record detail</a></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">Inline row edit</th>
            <td>one or two fields, and the user is scanning the list</td>
            <td>opening anything at all is too much ceremony — use <a href={base + '/components/inline-editing'}>M1</a></td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="bo-u-text-muted">
      On narrow screens the choice collapses: below the shell's breakpoint a side panel has
      nowhere to sit, so it becomes a full-width <a href={base + '/components/offcanvas'}>drawer</a>
      over the list. Design the panel so that works — one column, no side-by-side fields.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="demo">
    <h2>Anatomy</h2>
    <ol class="bo-stack bo-stack--tight docs-list">
      <li><strong>Master list</strong> — <a href={base + '/components/data-table'}>data table</a>;
        the row's first cell is a <code>&lt;th scope="row"&gt;</code> holding a real link, so the
        record is reachable, bookmarkable and openable in a new tab.</li>
      <li><strong>Selection state</strong> — <code>aria-selected</code> plus
        <code>data-row-state="selected"</code> on the <code>&lt;tr&gt;</code>. Two channels:
        the tint is visible, the attribute is programmatic.</li>
      <li><strong>Detail container</strong> — a <a href={base + '/components/dashboard#card'}>card</a>
        beside the list, or <a href={base + '/components/dialog'}>dialog</a>/<a href={base + '/components/offcanvas'}>offcanvas</a> over it.</li>
      <li><strong>Detail body</strong> — <a href={base + '/components/kv'}>key-value facts</a> to read,
        <a href={base + '/patterns/field-editor'}>the field editor</a> to write.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="demo">
    <h2>Data contract</h2>
    <div class="bo-data-table-container" tabindex="0">
      <table class="bo-data-table" data-density="compact">
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Request</th><th scope="col">Returns / on failure</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td class="bo-data-table__col--code">GET /vendors</td><td>the master list; the detail region renders empty until a row is chosen</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="bo-data-table__col--code">GET /vendors/:id</td><td><strong>the detail fragment only</strong>, swapped into the panel. Never re-render the list — that is what loses scroll position and selection</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="bo-data-table__col--code">PATCH /vendors/:id</td><td>the updated detail fragment, <em>and</em> the one changed row, so the list stays truthful without a reload (htmx: an out-of-band swap)</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="bo-data-table__col--code">404</td><td>the record vanished under the user — replace the panel with an empty state that says so and clears the selection</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="demo">
    <h2>States</h2>
    <div class="bo-data-table-container" tabindex="0">
      <table class="bo-data-table" data-density="compact">
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">State</th><th scope="col">What ships</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Nothing selected</td><td>the panel holds a one-line prompt, not a blank box — this is the screen's first impression</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Loading the detail</td><td><code>aria-busy</code> on the panel only; the list stays interactive so the user can pick a different row</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Empty list</td><td>the DIFFERENT empty when filters exclude everything: say which filter, and offer to clear it</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Detail 404</td><td>panel becomes an empty state; the row is deselected rather than left highlighted pointing at nothing</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Save conflict</td><td>409 in the panel with both values — see <a href={base + '/concepts/concurrency'}>concurrency</a>; nothing auto-merges</td></tr>
          <tr><td>No permission to edit</td><td>the panel reads; the Edit control is absent, not disabled</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Narrow screen</td><td>the panel becomes a drawer over the list; selection survives closing it</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="demo">
    <h2>Components used</h2>
    <p class="bo-u-text-muted"><span class="bo-badge">complexity 2 of 4</span></p>
    <ul class="bo-cluster docs-list-bare">
      <li><a class="bo-badge bo-badge--type" href={base + '/components/data-table'}>Data table</a></li>
      <li><a class="bo-badge bo-badge--type" href={base + '/components/dashboard#card'}>Card</a></li>
      <li><a class="bo-badge bo-badge--type" href={base + '/components/dialog'}>Dialog</a></li>
      <li><a class="bo-badge bo-badge--type" href={base + '/components/offcanvas'}>Drawers</a></li>
      <li><a class="bo-badge bo-badge--type" href={base + '/components/kv'}>Key-value facts</a></li>
      <li><a class="bo-badge bo-badge--type" href={base + '/components/badge'}>Badge</a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <script>
    import { initDialogs } from '@busy-office/ui/js';
    initDialogs();
  </script>

  <Related links={[
    ["/patterns/record-detail", "Record detail"],
    ["/patterns/field-editor", "Field editor"],
    ["/components/inline-editing", "Inline editing"],
    ["/concepts/concurrency", "Concurrency & conflicts"],
  ]} />
</Gallery>
